course: dictionary
lesson: 9453
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word staple is a good example: it can be a tiny wire, a verb, or a main food.
explain: «The potato was first farmed in the Andes of South America and became a staple food in Europe.» The clue is food, so a staple food must be a main food that people eat all the time. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Staples and drawing pins on the floor should be picked up, because bare feet and paws step on them.» The clues are floor, pins and feet, so this staple is the small metal wire kind, not a food.
fact: A staple can be a small piece of thin bent wire pushed through papers to hold them together.
fact: As a verb, «to staple» means to fasten things together with staples, as in «stapled the pages».
fact: A staple food is a basic food that people eat all the time, such as rice or bread.
fact: In geography, «staple foods» are the main foods of a place, such as rice in much of Asia.
fact: A staple can also be a U-shaped metal pin hammered into wood to hold a wire.
exercise: «Exercise books are made from big rolls of paper, cut, folded, stapled or glued along the spine.» What does stapled mean here? | Cut into tiny pieces | *Fastened together with small wire staples | Written in neat handwriting | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The potato became a staple food in Europe by the 1700s.» What does staple food mean? | A food that is rare and expensive | A food only eaten at parties | A food kept in a box for a special day | *A main food that people eat all the time
exercise: In a classroom, a stapler puts something into worksheets. What is it? | Paper clips | *Staples | Crayons | Glue sticks
test: Rice is the staple of many diets in Asia. What does staple mean here? | Very expensive | Made of metal | *Main or basic | Small and round
test: Ella needed to staple the pages together before school. What does staple mean here? | Lose and find again | *Fasten with staples | Draw a picture on | Read aloud to the class
exam: Mo says a staple is always a bent wire. Is he right? | Yes, but only in offices | No, a staple is always a bread | *No, a staple can also be a basic food | Yes, a staple is always a wire
